  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a **weighted** tree.\n\nThe distance from node xxx to node yyy is calculated as follows:\n\n\nLet there be kkk edges in the shortest path from node xxx to yyy.\nLet the weight of these edges, in the same **order** (from xxx to yyy), be denoted as e1,e2,…,eke_1, e_2, \\ldots, e_ke1​,e2​,…,ek​.\nThen, the distance from xxx to yyy is denoted as:\n\nd(x,y)=f(e1,0)⊕f(e2,1)⊕f(e3,2)⊕…⊕f(ek,k−1)d(x, y) = f(e_1, 0) \\oplus f(e_2, 1) \\oplus f(e_3, 2) \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus f(e_k, k-1)d(x,y)=f(e1​,0)⊕f(e2​,1)⊕f(e3​,2)⊕…⊕f(ek​,k−1), where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation, and\n\nf(a,b)f(a, b)f(a,b) denotes the integer obtained after bbb left circular shifts on the integer aaa (considering its 323232 bit binary representation).\n\nFor example, f((10000000000000000000000000000001)2,3)=(00000000000000000000000000001100)2f((10000000000000000000000000000001)_2,3) = (00000000000000000000000000001100)_2f((10000000000000000000000000000001)2​,3)=(00000000000000000000000000001100)2​.\nYour task is to find ∑v=1v=Nd(i,v)\\sum_{v = 1}^{v = N}d(i, v)∑v=1v=N​d(i,v) for each 1≤i≤N1\\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN — the number of nodes.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges. The ithi^{th}ith of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains three space-separated integers uiu_iui​, viv_ivi​ and wiw_iwi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​ of weight wiw_iwi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a single line, NNN space-separated integers, ∑v=1v=Nd(i,v)\\sum_{v = 1}^{v = N}d(i, v)∑v=1v=N​d(i,v) for each 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N,ui≠vi1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N, u_i \\neq v_i1≤ui​,vi​≤N,ui​=vi​",
      "1≤wi≤1091 \\leq w_i \\leq 10^91≤wi​≤109",
      "It is guaranteed that the input forms a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
